window.kycLocalMeasuresOH = {"39035":{"state":"OH","name":"Cuyahoga County","read":"2026-11-01","office":{"name":"Cuyahoga County Board of Elections","url":"https://boe.cuyahogacounty.gov/"},"own":{"status":"listed","measures":[{"j":"Cuyahoga County","jk":"county","designation":"Issue 10","title":"Proposed Tax Levy (Additional) Board of Developmental Disabilities - County of Cuyahoga","kind":"Tax","source":"https://boe.cuyahogacounty.gov/elections/GetDocumentById/0ed80c8b-5b7d-46d5-b60f-91a47eea555b/","sourceTitle":"November 3, 2026 General Election Issues List","read":"2026-11-01","text":"A majority affirmative vote is necessary for passage. An additional tax for the benefit of the County of Cuyahoga for the purpose of the operation of community programs and services authorized by county boards of developmental disabilities, for the acquisition, construction, renovation, financing, maintenance, and operation of developmental disabilities facilities, or for both of such purposes, that the County Fiscal Officer estimates will collect $99,684,616 annually, at a rate not exceeding 2.25 mills for each $1 of taxable value, which amounts to $79 for each $100,000 of the County Fiscal Officer’s market value, for ten years, commencing in 2026, first due in calendar year 2027."},{"j":"Cuyahoga County","jk":"county","designation":"Issue 11","title":"Proposed Tax Levy (Renewal and Increase) Health and Human Services - County of Cuyahoga","kind":"Tax","source":"https://boe.cuyahogacounty.gov/elections/GetDocumentById/0ed80c8b-5b7d-46d5-b60f-91a47eea555b/","sourceTitle":"November 3, 2026 General Election Issues List","read":"2026-11-01","text":"A majority affirmative vote is necessary for passage. A renewal of 4.7 mills and an increase of 2.5 mills for each $1 of taxable value to constitute a tax for the benefit of the County of Cuyahoga for the purpose of supplementing general fund appropriations for health and human or social services, that the County Fiscal Officer estimates will collect $261,527,652 annually, at a rate not exceeding 7.2 mills for each $1 of taxable value, which amounts to $196 for each $100,000 of the County Fiscal Officer’s market value, for ten years, commencing in 2026, first due in calendar year 2027."},{"j":"Cuyahoga County","jk":"county","designation":"Issue 12","title":"Proposed Charter Amendment - County of Cuyahoga","kind":"Charter amendment","source":"https://boe.cuyahogacounty.gov/elections/GetDocumentById/0ed80c8b-5b7d-46d5-b60f-91a47eea555b/","sourceTitle":"November 3, 2026 General Election Issues List","read":"2026-11-01","text":"A majority affirmative vote is necessary for passage. Shall Article II, Section 2.03 and Article VI, Section 6.04 of the Charter of the County of Cuyahoga be amended to require that County Council confirm the County Executive’s removal of members of boards, agencies, commissions and authorities as are or may hereafter be created by or pursuant to the Charter, as are provided by general law to be appointed by boards of county commissioners, and on special boards and commissions created by any agreement with another public agency or court order?"},{"j":"Cuyahoga County","jk":"county","designation":"Issue 13","title":"Proposed Charter Amendment - County of Cuyahoga","kind":"Charter amendment","source":"https://boe.cuyahogacounty.gov/elections/GetDocumentById/0ed80c8b-5b7d-46d5-b60f-91a47eea555b/","sourceTitle":"November 3, 2026 General Election Issues List","read":"2026-11-01","text":"A majority affirmative vote is necessary for passage. Shall Article V, Section 5.06 of the Charter of the County of Cuyahoga be amended to provide that the Director of Law shall provide primary legal representation on labor negotiations, grievances and arbitrations, non-litigation related employment matters, public records matters, risk management functions and activities, and non-litigation related contracts, agreements, debt issuance documents, memoranda of understanding, purchase orders, and other legal instruments entered into by the County Executive on behalf of Cuyahoga County; that the powers and duties of the Director of Law shall include giving written opinions and other legal advice to the Executive, County Council, officers, departments, directors, boards, agencies, commissions, and authorities appointed or established under the various Articles of the Charter, and other County entities whose chief executive officers serve at the pleasure of the County Executive or County Council; that nothing prohibits the County Executive, County Council or other entities established by Charter, Council, or general law, from seeking or obtaining advice from the Prosecuting Attorney; that this Section 5.06 shall not in any way limit the powers and duties of the Prosecuting Attorney as set forth in Section 4.01 and general law; and that in no event shall the Director of Law prosecute, defend, appear in court, or otherwise handle any action in any litigation or litigation-related proceedings on behalf of the County or any of its entities, unless referred to the Law Director by the Prosecuting Attorney?"},{"j":"Cuyahoga County","jk":"county","designation":"Issue 14","title":"Proposed Charter Amendment - County of Cuyahoga","kind":"Charter amendment","source":"https://boe.cuyahogacounty.gov/elections/GetDocumentById/0ed80c8b-5b7d-46d5-b60f-91a47eea555b/","sourceTitle":"November 3, 2026 General Election Issues List","read":"2026-11-01","text":"A majority affirmative vote is necessary for passage. Shall Article XII, Section 12.09 of the Charter of the County of Cuyahoga be amended to provide that four (4) members of the Charter Review Commission shall be appointed by the County Executive, and such appointments shall not be subject to Council confirmation; four (4) members shall be appointed by the Council, and such appointments shall not be presented to the County Executive for approval or disapproval; and that one (1) member shall be appointed by the County Executive, subject to confirmation by Council?"}]},"cities":[{"status":"unlisted","basis":{"from":"list","url":"https://boe.cuyahogacounty.gov/elections/GetDocumentById/0ed80c8b-5b7d-46d5-b60f-91a47eea555b/","title":"November 3, 2026 General Election Issues List","found":"lists no question of the City of Cleveland as a whole; its Cleveland entries are six single-precinct liquor options"},"name":"City of Cleveland","place":"3916000"}]},"39049":{"state":"OH","name":"Franklin County","read":"2026-11-01","office":{"name":"Franklin County Board of Elections","url":"https://vote.franklincountyohio.gov/home"},"own":{"status":"unlisted","basis":{"from":"list","url":"https://vote.franklincountyohio.gov/getmedia/4001b052-1b90-4f73-b030-2d981e6ec8fa/2026-General-Certified-Questions-and-Issues","title":"Certified Questions and Issues, November 3, 2026 General Election","found":"lists issues of cities, townships, villages and school districts, and none of Franklin County or a countywide district"}},"cities":[{"status":"listed","measures":[{"j":"City of Columbus","jk":"city","designation":"#8","title":"Columbus – Proposed Charter Amendment (by petition)","kind":"Charter amendment","source":"https://vote.franklincountyohio.gov/getmedia/258ab3a2-ddef-42a8-a869-c38b6c068a06/Notice-of-Election-Columbus-Charter-Amendment-1-Petition","sourceTitle":"Notice of Election on Proposition: Columbus Charter Amendment (by petition)","read":"2026-11-01","place":"3918000","text":"This proposed charter amendment would limit the ability to vote for candidates for Columbus City Council to only those electors living within the districts that those candidates seek to represent. The amendment specifies that ballots within council districts will include both citywide races as well as the district race. The amendment allows for the initiation of a recall election of a council district representative if a petition is submitted bearing the signatures of the electors of that district in an amount that is at least fifteen (15%) percent of the votes cast within the district in the preceding mayoral election. Shall the proposed charter amendment be approved?"},{"j":"City of Columbus","jk":"city","designation":"#9","title":"Columbus – Proposed Charter Amendment (by Council)","kind":"Charter amendment","source":"https://vote.franklincountyohio.gov/getmedia/a3d9d75e-83ff-492a-98c4-a8cc09e1cd60/Notice-of-Election-Columbus-Charter-Amendment-2-Council","sourceTitle":"Notice of Election on Proposition: Columbus Charter Amendment (by Council)","read":"2026-11-01","place":"3918000","text":"This proposed charter amendment would limit the ability to vote for candidates for Columbus City Council to only those electors living within the districts that those candidates seek to represent. The amendment adds two (2) at-large council representatives to be elected in 2027 and seated in 2028, and an additional two (2) atlarge council representatives to be elected in 2029 and seated in 2030. All at-large council representatives will be elected for four (4) year terms. The amendment includes provisions for transitioning from the current nine (9) member Council to an eleven (11) member Council and then subsequently to a thirteen (13) member Council, allowing for the ongoing staggering of terms. The amendment allows councilmembers representing districts whose boundaries are redrawn but who still have at least two years remaining in their term to serve the remainder of their term representing a newly-drawn district. The amendment specifies that candidates for council district seats must have resided within their district for at least one year prior to the primary election. The amendment calls for a redraw of the current council district map to occur in 2027, and increases the maximum population variance between districts from 1% to 7.5%. The amendment updates the vote requirements for expelling and/or removing councilmembers for misconduct, malfeasance, misfeasance, or nonfeasance. The amendment updates the expulsion vote threshold for conduct from “six” to “2/3rds,” and the expulsion vote for absences from “three-fifths” to “2/3rds.” The amendment updates the charter to reflect the minimum number of councilmembers necessary to achieve a quorum for the purposes of meeting for business. The amendment increases the number of affirmative votes that would be needed to adopt ordinances or resolutions in concert with expanding the size of the legislature. The amendment specifies that candidates for district councilmember must collect at least 150 signatures of electors from within their district, and that at-large candidates must collect at least 250 signatures of electors from within the city limits. The amendment specifies that ballots within council districts will include both citywide races as well as the district race. The amendment allows for the initiation of a recall election of a council district representative if a petition is submitted bearing the signatures of the electors of that district in an amount equal to or greater than fifteen (15%) percent of the votes cast within the district in the preceding mayoral election. The amendment allows for the initiation of a recall election of an at-large representative if a petition is submitted bearing the signatures of the electors citywide in an amount equal to or greater than fifteen (15%) percent of the votes cast within the district in the preceding mayoral election. Shall the proposed charter amendment be approved?"}],"name":"City of Columbus","place":"3918000"}]}};
